.TH SUPIVPN-MIGRATE 8 "October 2026" "SupiVPN" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
supivpn-migrate \- explicitly apply SupiVPN database migrations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn-migrate
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies the migrations embedded in this build using a separate database owner
identity. Review schema compatibility and backups before invoking it.
Package installation and controller startup never run this command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Non-secret AWS migration configuration. Without it, use SUPIVPN_DATABASE_URL.
.TP
.BI \-expected-schema-sha256 " digest"
Require the expected SQL source digest from provisioning.
.TP
.BI \-public-role " name"
Pre-created restricted public database login.
.TP
.BI \-agent-role " name"
Pre-created restricted agent database login.
.TP
.BI \-recovery-role " name"
Pre-created restricted recovery database login.
.TP
.B \-h
Show command-line help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUPIVPN_DATABASE_URL
Database connection string for the migration owner identity.
Supply it through a protected process environment, never command-line
arguments or a committed file. Do not reuse it for the controller runtime.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/supivpn-controller/migrations/
contains inspection copies of embedded SQL. Do not edit or apply these files
individually.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR supivpn-controller (8)
.br
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-controller/POSTGRES.md.gz
